}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-21T19:40:39-08:00","id":34723,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, the quality of the glyph fonts is poor. I assume it's because there's a limited umber of vectors within that font.<br /> There is a way I've been acquiring them, but, for now, that's a trade secret. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","user":"Torakhan","date":". 12-21-2013, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T03:37:08-08:00","id":34876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=34723#post34723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, the quality of the glyph fonts is poor. I assume it's because there's a limited umber of vectors within that font.<br /> There is a way I've been acquiring them, but, for now, that's a trade secret. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it is that bad, considering I've been getting pretty good results from the font, myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:26:45-08:00","id":37338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=19107#post19107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When I had to use Ghural Glyphs I made them very blocky and square versions of Garou glyphs. Thicker too.<br /> <br /> oo care you share your created glyphs? maybe we can compile our own pictogram library of suggestions and have Onyx Path sign off on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are all great glyphs. I'd like to see your Gurahl glyphs, if you wouldn't mind, they being my favorite of the Fera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T19:42:41-08:00","id":37624,"title":"","content":"Grim: I can tell by your avatar. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'll try and draw some out and take a photo. Just picture Garou glyphs bigger, thicker and no curves. That's now I made the bear style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T17:53:40-08:00","id":38090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=34701#post34701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, there is a glyph font (Doesn't have everything though). It's Werewolf bats or dingbats, but it is cool to have it on Microsoft word.<br /> You can find it on <a href=\"http://righttodream.digitaldreaming.org/downloads.html\" target=\"_blank\">The Right to Dream page</a>.<br /> <br /> I recently did glyphs for the <a href=\"http://ajabahyena.tumblr.com/post/69214511698/fallen-fera-glyphs\" target=\"_blank\">Fallen Fera</a>. Most of the names come from Book of the Wyrm or MET Book of the Wyrm. Those that didn't have names, I had to come up with some. Will be interesting to see this all covered in Book of the Wyrm 20th.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have seen and own those fonts, but I was hoping for something, well, official and more complete. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T05:10:02-07:00","id":119046,"title":"","content":"Sooooort of related:<br /> <br /> I'm putting together a compiled glyph reference, to host all official and custom glyphs that I can find (and get permission for). In the case of official oWoD glyphs, I've found that even the very comprehensive sites like the already-mentioned <a href=\"http://glyphmaker.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Glyphs Dictionar</a><a href=\"http://glyphmaker.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\">y</a>, <a href=\"http://www.badgersden.com/MT/GarouGlyphs/Garou.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Badgers Den</a>, and the others, never seem to have every glyph; obscure ones tend to be left out in every case. As far as custom, so far I am not aware of a site that showcases more than ones used for their own games (which is fine!) or on-request.<br /> <br /> So, my intention is put all of them in one place, so the intricate glyph stories of <a href=\"http://sabertooth1980.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sabertooth1980</a>, the Mokol\u00e9 auspice glyphs of <a href=\"http://www.flickr.com/photos/rosaumbra/\" target=\"_blank\">Rosaumbra</a>, glyph names of <a href=\"http://traveling-star.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Traveling-Star</a>, and many others, can can be displayed next to each other for ease of viewing and friendly comparison of style.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, rather than try to hunt down every individual glyph-designer of this forum, I'd like to make a general call for people who want to participate and include their glyphs in the compilation to either reply here or PM me with links to the glyphs they want to include, any descriptions to go with it, and preference of crediting (what name to attribute, and what URL to link back to).<br /> <br /> The site is not up yet, as I'm still figuring out if I want to use webs.com for it given its limitations, but at the moment the plan is that they will be at glyphery.webs.com.<br /> <br /> (Sorry for the deleted post, I couldn't get it to remove the unwanted link otherwise.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T02:42:45-07:00","id":121588,"title":"","content":"This sounds really cool. I was hoping someone would be able to do this. See the previous posts about my copyright questions. I would like to contribute, but I do not have an easy or scanable means to submit my custom glyph work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T03:01:37-07:00","id":121594,"title":"","content":"I've e-mailed Onyx Path about the permissions/copyright. I imagine it will be a while before I hear back (low priority and all), but once I know what I need to display for the legal purposes, the official glyphs will go up and I can share whatever they say. I'm pretty sure there won't be issues, though; back when sanctioned White Wolf fan sites were a huge thing, they had a legalese blurb you could just copy and paste onto your site, like Mox has, and some restrictions on how they could be displayed.<br /> <br /> Also! If your glyphs are hard copy but not scanned, you could even take pictures (if that's an option) of your glyphs and I could do whatever cropping or editing might be needed, if you don't have a program for it. Or whatever other help you might need for it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":". 04-29-2014, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T09:22:32-07:00","id":123212,"title":"","content":"A shot in the dark here: does anyone happen to know a way to contact Glenn Moyer (<a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/rosaumbra/\" target=\"_blank\">Rosaumbra on Flickr</a>) other than through his Flickr? I'm not certain how often he might check his mail there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:31:47-07:00","id":124146,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen them sorry. No idea how to contact them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T20:42:18-07:00","id":146293,"title":"","content":"I was joking the other night about how Rokea &quot;glyphs&quot; would all look like shark bites, and the meaning based on how deep and how many bites were made:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> One bite / light impressions: &quot;I am curious / What is this?&quot;<br /> Two bites / deeper impressions: &quot;I am interested in this / this reacted!&quot;<br /> Three bites / more+deeper impressions: Intensifying degree of &quot;This is threatening / this is delicious.&quot;</div> <br /> Naturally, these glyphs would be temporary in nature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I bugged all the official e-mails about getting legal permission again, partially because I'm not sure if I was bugging the correct one before. I'm almost done with the collection of glyphs from those I've already asked, and then I'll be hunting for fresh blood to contribute to <a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\">the Cyber Record</a>. Laughing Hyena is currently dominating in sheer amount of glyphs, someone needs to honorably challenge her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm not paying for hosting yet, so my format and presentation options are still limited. When I go pay and get unlimited pages to use, I'll be able to better organize and give everything its own section, including having sort options such as &quot;by contributor&quot;. Right now I'm limited to about 10 pages, I think, of which I am using 7, and I can't use any non-prefabricated HTML; everything is their pre-fab templates. If people are willing to keep these restrictions in mind, I'd love to hear their feedback on how I could organize the glyphs better, especially in regards to layout and size of the images. The categories are still a bit in flux. The actual prettiness of the site isn't a high priority for me so much as the usability of it, although it should be getting some preening soon.<br /> <br /> Has anyone worked on any Breed-style-specific glyphs, like the Bastet 'swirlies' or the Corax 'peck-and-scratches'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T23:21:01-07:00","id":148430,"title":"","content":"Ha! I guess I'm going to have to challenge Laughing... Times like this I wish I had a wacom or some other drawing tablet. I really can't do the drawings of glyphs otherwise. In fact I don't even think the ones I do draw look very close to the jagged style that WW has created. Yakecen, I'm wondering if maybe Patreon might be a way to go for funding hosting options. That way if say a contributor wants to see their stuff archived they can help with Patreon. Or myabe just a regular donations button.<br /> <br /> on other topics I mentioned once before about making ghural style glyphs as blockier thicker versions of Garou glyphs. My notes and test sheets look horrible since they're all done with a huge chisel marker, but it got the idea across. I've always imagined people who can write calligraphy should try their hand at Bastet glyphs and since I don't know calligraphy I've been too chicken to try myself. Corax glyphs I thought should incorporate Poop splats as well as peck holes and scratches... Good ideas on the Rokea bite marks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> maybe the Mokole would have a similar system. Would the Ananasi use Charlotte's Web type making their versions of glyphs? There's a thought...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T01:16:05-07:00","id":148523,"title":"","content":"I like the Ananasi message-web idea a lot. I imagine something like that could be pretty subtle, too; not something that is necessarily read with the eyes so much as leaving trails of silk that can be felt, and the tension or angle of the silk conveys a particular message. Like a silent stringed instrumental, tactile rather than aural, and more like road-signs than conversation tools. Oh man, thoughts of Ananasi guzheng players, orchestrating near-silent movements like the creepers they are.<br /> <br /> Good idea about the donation thing, I'd considered adding something like that as an option, but I wasn't sure if it would be worth the implementation. Haha. Once I'm getting a steady paycheck, it won't be an issue anyway.<br /> <br /> I also had an idea of starting up an archive of characters that people could make submissions to, although I'm not sure if other people would be as excited about something like that as I am. Maybe Wiki style. I love archiving and saving things, and I think it'd be neat to have a sort of living history of characters, PCs or NPCs, that other people can read about; and their little dossier page on the Cyber Record could link to any other stories their player might have for them, or something else pertaining, so people who don't design custom glyphs can still participate, if they want. It would also fit the pseudo-IC theme of the Cyber Record being an Information Geomid that delights in collecting this particular data!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T19:44:22-07:00","id":149087,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me now that we really need a Werewolf Claw paintbrush for photoshop. Does anyone know if such a thing exists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T20:37:27-07:00","id":149104,"title":"","content":"Not I. I'll search around, though. ( <a href=\"http://all-free-download.com/photoshop-brushes/paw_prints_bird_footprints_and_stuff_each_brush_39368.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://all-free-download.com/photosh...ush_39368.html</a> This looks kind of neat? Not claw marks, but animal prints.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T02:32:11-07:00","id":149262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=149087#post149087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurs to me now that we really need a Werewolf Claw paintbrush for photoshop. Does anyone know if such a thing exists?</div> </div> </div> </div>Straightforward to make (loads of tutorials out there). Not sure how useful it'll be though as the glyph clawmarks don't seem to be very consistent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T08:53:46-07:00","id":149422,"title":"","content":"My search yeilded a lot of how to make paintbrushes that were more like stamps really or brushes to make fur effects. A friend of mine who's an art major studying computer animation tells me that it is completely possible to make a paintbrush that is a solid color with periodic little indents like the kind we see in the glyphs. Course, she's working with Wacoms and Cintiques and all kinds of programs where she knows how to program what she needs into her pallet. I don't. I know nothing about programming languages aside from some basic HTML.<br /> <br /> In researching it a bit more, for it to really work like the claw made glyphs it would have to be something programmed for a pressure sensitive tablet that gives you a round starting point and taper off to a point. the little jagged indents would have to resize according to the thickness of the 'brushstroke'. It is possible, but more complex than the typical photoshop brush creating tutorials that I've been looking at. If anyone knows of a tutorial that is building what I'm describing, please point me in the right direction.<br /> <br /> If this doesn't exist I'll see if I can find someone who knows what they're doing to create it and share this brush with everyone who has a compatible program. It'd be great to make it a universal tool. It'd make creating custom Glyphs so easy. It's that or someone with Much more programming capability could make a Create Your Own program out of Flash to put together single glyph shapes layered and sized until you export the finished product as a single image. If people can make their own dress up dolls, South Park characters or Ponies using those programs, it should be possible for a glyph layering program. I wish I knew how to make such things, but I don't. Maybe there's a tutorial out there for those kinds of programs too, but I'm afraid I don't have the time or even an art program other than Paint to work with for creating those basic graphics. Maybe someone else here does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T05:30:29-07:00","id":150193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=149422#post149422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In researching it a bit more, for it to really work like the claw made glyphs it would have to be something programmed for a pressure sensitive tablet that gives you a round starting point and taper off to a point. the little jagged indents would have to resize according to the thickness of the 'brushstroke'. It is possible, but more complex than the typical photoshop brush creating tutorials that I've been looking at. If anyone knows of a tutorial that is building what I'm describing, please point me in the right direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.photoshopessentials.com/basics/photoshop-brushes/make-brushes/\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> seems pretty close to what you're describing. Capture the nicks in your brush pattern then start with high pressure, ease off when you want to taper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=149422#post149422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If this doesn't exist I'll see if I can find someone who knows what they're doing to create it and share this brush with everyone who has a compatible program. It'd be great to make it a universal tool. It'd make creating custom Glyphs so easy. It's that or someone with Much more programming capability could make a Create Your Own program out of Flash to put together single glyph shapes layered and sized until you export the finished product as a single image. If people can make their own dress up dolls, South Park characters or Ponies using those programs, it should be possible for a glyph layering program. I wish I knew how to make such things, but I don't. Maybe there's a tutorial out there for those kinds of programs too, but I'm afraid I don't have the time or even an art program other than Paint to work with for creating those basic graphics. Maybe someone else here does.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue with automated layering is that complex layered glyphs tend to look really quite bad. Some sort of merging or alteration is necessary to make them clear. When playing around with them myself, the two following (though not &quot;technically&quot; correct) things have made them easier for players to read and better looking 1) incorporate glyphs into the design while avoiding overlay, or 2) shifting the colour shades to indicate order in which the glyphs are carved and depth (so a simple two glyph combination might be grey and black).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","user":"Obyrne","date":". 05-27-2014, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T05:29:42-07:00","id":151215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Obyrne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=150193#post150193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.photoshopessentials.com/basics/photoshop-brushes/make-brushes/\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> seems pretty close to what you're describing. Capture the nicks in your brush pattern then start with high pressure, ease off when you want to taper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the issue with automated layering is that complex layered glyphs tend to look really quite bad. Some sort of merging or alteration is necessary to make them clear. When playing around with them myself, the two following (though not &quot;technically&quot; correct) things have made them easier for players to read and better looking 1) incorporate glyphs into the design while avoiding overlay, or 2) shifting the colour shades to indicate order in which the glyphs are carved and depth (so a simple two glyph combination might be grey and black).</div> </div> </div> </div>With a Create your own Program like I was describing you would not be able to make complex epic glyph sagas. There wouldn't even be complex glyphs in the library. It would be pretty basic One Mark per layer type of thing. A Curved slash left to right. Curved slash right to left. Curved gouge left, Curved gourge right, Moon circle, etc. We'd have to use only the pieces that make up the standard glyphs, otherwise we'd run into the copyright issue. Slider bars could control the length and thickness of a given mark. Another slider could control the Opacity and make it solid black or a lighter gray as you suggested. Another slider could let you rotate the layer around. It wouldn't be able to handle long epic sagas, no... but it would be good to build your own name glyph or an easy tool to make signpost glyphs for Cearns or Packs or your own Totem spirits. If you Really wanted to create a saga, I guess one could create a bunch of sections of the story in glyph form from the Maker Program and export them as one image and then put those smaller image files together in a better program like Adobe. But then you might as well build the whole epic in Adobe anyways...<br /> <br /> Anyways, my idea was just for a quick and easy tool program like a die roller or a char sheet random NPC generator. I don't have the skills for it, but with so many Make Your Own Doll programs out there it seemed like something that would be possible for someone who knows what they are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":1332,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","user":"Darling_Rose","date":".  I forgot to feed the monkeys... 05-28-2014, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:54:02-07:00","id":151602,"title":"","content":"Illustrator and other vector programs may be a better place to find a &quot;brush&quot; that works. Unfortunately, it also really needs either randomness in the brush (so that two strokes next to each other don't look the same), or a whole group of brushes that can be used and chosen from.<br /> Like, 20 that start blunt, and end sharp, and 20 that start sharp and end sharp.<br /> SOME vector programs are also pressure-sensitive. This would be the best sort of program to use as well.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I don't think that a Photoshop paintbrush is quite going to give the same style of &quot;texture&quot; that Rich created back in 1992 and continued to be the style from then on. Then again, maybe something that is more, er, &quot;natural&quot; in its outline/silhouette may work better if we wanted it to be more &quot;Realistic&quot;?<br /> <br /> So, yeah... my suggestion would be to look at a vector program--not only would it be able to create the contours that you're looking for, but then it would be in vector format.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T13:15:40-07:00","id":151618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=151602#post151602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I don't think that a Photoshop paintbrush is quite going to give the same style of &quot;texture&quot; that Rich created back in 1992 and continued to be the style from then on. Then again, maybe something that is more, er, &quot;natural&quot; in its outline/silhouette may work better if we wanted it to be more &quot;Realistic&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly, in one of the Darker Days Radio podcasts there was an interview that mentioned that the glyphs were created by taping sharpie pens/markers around each finger as a &quot;claw&quot;. So the hand could make claw-like markings with each marker on a finger.<br /> <br /> I've been also looking up Bastet glyphs, but no one has really created anything with them. Corax, are probably best with a few simple concepts with their glyphs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T14:09:01-07:00","id":151665,"title":"","content":"If there's any software tools for drawing Chinese calligraphy, specifying brushstrokes as vectors, that would probably work great as a base for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T17:08:17-07:00","id":151833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=151665#post151665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's any software tools for drawing Chinese calligraphy, specifying brushstrokes as vectors, that would probably work great as a base for this.</div> </div> </div> </div> Those were the kind of brushes I was thinking of. I've seen them in use before, but couldn't remember the program. They can be programmed with a randomized formula for the characteristics of paint or marker so why not randomized jagged bits in claw marks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:52:23-07:00","id":154194,"title":"","content":"What do you do if you have different looking fan-made glyphs of the same thing? It's more awkward when both artists can see which you've picked and you know them. Do you choose the one from the player that's been around longer? Or go with the aesthetic newb? Should the group vote which they like better and make that one the &quot;official&quot; one? Or throw both out and make your own as the ST? <br /> <br /> This may also apply to the glyph archive as well some day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:30:40-07:00","id":154225,"title":"","content":"Why would you need to pick one? Call them synonyms, or regional variations. It may be just one language but there's no reason there can't be SOME cases of multiple glyphs for the same meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T15:35:21-07:00","id":154227,"title":"","content":"Unless one isn't very good, alter the meanings slightly and use both. So long as they're close enough in meaning, it just gives you a wider range of ways to say things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/836-obyrne","name":"Obyrne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T22:44:11-07:00","id":154554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/18714-garou-glyphs?p=154194#post154194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you do if you have different looking fan-made glyphs of the same thing? It's more awkward when both artists can see which you've picked and you know them. Do you choose the one from the player that's been around longer? Or go with the aesthetic newb? Should the group vote which they like better and make that one the &quot;official&quot; one? Or throw both out and make your own as the ST?<br /> <br /> This may also apply to the glyph archive as well some day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Post both, IMO. There's really no reason to choose, because in the case of the Cyber Record, it's less about establishing an expanded lexicon than it is showing off how people have approached, interpreted, and put their own methods of thought into the pictograms; which means neither is really more valid than the other. There are some custom glyphs that I don't &quot;agree&quot; with, in the sense that I would have gone about it from a different perspective, but that's what makes it interesting also; I didn't think about it from that way. How might a lupus, metis, and homid think about this concept? How might it look different, as a result? If you asked each breed to create a glyph that encompasses their feeling and intent behind a concept, I bet each one would make something that looks different, even if there is a common theme.<br /> <br /> For instance, Laughing Hyena has a bunch of Weaver concepts. If someone else has glyphs for a television or a car they want to contribute, I'll be posting those up as well. One set might appeal to one person or type of character more than the other.<br /> <br /> Personally, I post up everything I receive. Some are still pending because they're waiting for the artist to send me a few more details, or how they want to be credited, or I'm just figuring out how to arrange them. (LH has a bunch of Hengeyokai glyphs I'm not entirely sure how I want to sort. Do I want to give them their own section? Do I want to split them up between the Rank, Renown, and Auspice sections? 3 in a row, or 4? Or should I try to squeeze 6 in a row? Hrrrrng.) But yeah, there's no reason to choose. The official glyphs can have lots of different implicit meaning, after all. The new moon symbol means Ragabash, but it could also be used to any of the themes attributed to the Ragabash, like stealth, questioning, trickery. Philodox could be used for anything having to do with laws, judgement. Even the simple Gaia symbol is both the entirety of the Earth Mother concept, as well as just the physical earth or land, and it is the core shape modified to mean life or death, and many others. I think that 'core concept' ... well, concept, with glyphs is part of what makes it so fun, interesting, and versatile. Context is what fills in the rest of a details between two very similar looking glyphs that mean different things, as well as the impression the whole symbol together gives, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":".  Typos! 05-31-2014, 06:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T06:17:51-07:00","id":161608,"title":"","content":"As of now, all the custom glyphs that I've been sent or have been given green light to post up are on the Cyber Record - including the latest from Darling_Rose, such as her Yeren glyph. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which means I'm on the hunt again! (Toooooorakhaaaaaaan.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T23:28:24-07:00","id":225702,"title":"","content":"My activity here has sort of gone to a crawl since my schedule is a bit in flux at work, but I still got time to do weekly glyph uploads if any of y'all have some more custom ones you want to add to the Record. Just e-mail them to <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#4135292422382324333324222e332501262c20282d6f222e2c\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"daaeb2bfb9a3b8bfa8a8bfb9b5a8be9abdb7bbb3b6f4b9b5b7\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> along with any description or other info you might want included, and I'll get them up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divid